iameter MA): (x-21/8)²+(y-5√7/8)²=23/8.\n\nSubtract: \n[(x-3)²-(x-21/8)²] + [(y-√7/7)²-(y-5√7/8)²] = 64/7-23/8.\n\n(x-3)²-(x-21/8)² = [(x-3)-(x-21/8)][(x-3)+(x-21/8)] = [-3+21/8][2x-3-21/8] = [-24/8+21/8][2x-45/8] = (-3/8)(2x-45/8).\n\n(y-√7/7)²-(y-5√7/8)² = [(y-√7/7)-(y-5√7/8)][(y-√7/7)+(y-5√7/8)] = [5√7/8-√7/7][2y-√7/7-5√7/8].\n5√7/8-√7/7 = √7(5/8-1/7)=√7(35-8)/56=27√7/56.\n√7/7+5√7/8 = √7(1/7+5/8)=√7(8+35)/56=43√7/56.\nSo this = (27√7/56)(2y-43√7/56).\n\nRHS = 64/7-23/8 = (512-161)/56=351/56.\n\nSo: (-3/8)(2x-45/8) + (27√7/56)(2y-43√7/56) = 351/56.\n\nMultiply by 56:\n(-3/8)(56)(2x-45/8) + 27√7(2y-43√7/56) = 351.\n(-21)(2x-45/8) + 27√7(2y) - 27√7·43√7/56 = 351.\n-42x + 21·45/8 + 54√7 y - 27·43·7/56 = 351.\n21·45/8 = 945/8.\n27·43·7/56 = 27·301/56 = 8127/56.\n\n-42x + 945/8 + 54√7 y - 8127/56 = 351.\nConvert to /56: 945/8=6615/56. \n-42x + 54√7 y + 6615/56 - 8127/56 = 351.\n6615-8127 = -1512. -1512/56 = -27.\n-42x + 54√7 y - 27 = 351.\n-42x + 54√7 y = 378.\nDivide by 6: -7x + 9√7 y = 63.\nSo 9√7 y = 7x+63, y = (7x+63)/(9√7) = 7(x+9)/(9√7).\n\nThis is the radical axis (line through A and P). Let me verify A=(9/4, 5√7/4) is on it:\n7(9/4+9)/(9√7) = 7(9/4+36/4)/(9√7)=7(45/4)/(9√7)=315/(36√7)=35/(4√7)=35√7/28=5√7/4. ✓.\n\nSo line AP: y = 7(x+9)/(9√7). P is the other intersection of this line with the circumcircle.\n\nParametrize: substitute y into circumcircle (x-3)²+(y-√7/7)²=64/7.\ny-√7/7 = 7(x+9)/(9√7) - √7/7 = [7(x+9)·7 - 9√7·√7]/(9√7·7)... let me compute carefully.\n= 7(x+9)/(9√7) - √7/7.\nCommon denominator 63√7: 7(x+9)·7/(63√7) - √7·9√7/(63√7) = 49(x+9)/(63√7) - 9·7/(63√7) = [49(x+9)-63]/(63√7) = [49x+441-63]/(63√7) = [49x+378]/(63√7) = 7(7x+54)/(63√7) = (7x+54)/(9√7).\n\nSo (y-√7/7)² = (7x+54)²/(81·7) = (7x+54)²/567.\n\n(x-3)² = x²-6x+9.\n\nx²-6x+9 + (7x+54)²/567 = 64/7.\nMultiply by 567: 567x²-3402x+5103 + (7x+54)² = 64·81 = 5184.\n(7x+54)²=49x²+756x+2916.\n567x²+49x²=616x². -3402x+756x=-2646x. 5103+2916=8019.\n616x²-2646x+8019 = 5184.\n616x²-2646x+2835=0.\nDivide by... gcd? 616=8·77=8·7·11. 2646=2·1323=2·3·441=2·3·21²=2·3·441. 2835=5·567=5·81·7=2835. Hmm gcd maybe 7? 616/7=88, 2646/7=378, 2835/7=405. Yes!\n88x²-378x+405=0.\nDiscriminant: 378²-4·88·405 = 142884-142560=324=18².\nx = (378±18)/(176).\nx = 396/176 = 99/44 = 9/4 (that's A), or x = 360/176 = 45/22.\n\nSo P has x=45/22. y = 7(45/22+9)/(9√7) = 7(45/22+198/22)/(9√7)=7(243/22)/(9√7)=1701/(198√7)=1701/(198√7). Simplify 1701/198: divide by 9: 189/22. So y=189/(22√7)=189√7/(22·7)=189√7/154=27√7/22.\n\nSo P = (45/22, 27√7/22).\n\nLet me verify P on circumcircle: (45/22-3)²+(27√7/22-√7/7)².\n45/22-3=45/22-66/22=-21/22. (-21/22)²=441/484.\n27√7/22-√7/7 = √7(27/22-1/7)=√7(189-22)/154=167√7/154. \nHmm let me recompute: 27/22-1/7=(189-22)/154=167/154. So (167√7/154)²=167²·7/154²=27889·7/23716=195223/23716.\n441/484 = 441·49/23716=21609/23716.\nSum=(21609+195223)/23716=216832/23716. 216832/23716... 23716·9=213444. 216832-213444=3388. 3388/23716... hmm should be 64/7=64·3388/23716... 64/7 = 64·3388/(7·3388)... let me just check 216832/23716 vs 64/7. 64/7=64·3388/23716=216832/23716. ✓ \n\nNow find D: foot of perpendicular from B=(0,0) to line AC.\nA=(9/4,5√7/4), C=(6,0). Direction AC = C-A = (6-9/4, -5√7/4) = (15/4, -5√7/4) = (5/4)(3,-√7).\nLine AC: parametrize as A + t(C-A). D = A + t(C-A) where (D-B)·(C-A)=0, i.e., D·(C-A)=0.\nD = (9/4 + 15t/4, 5√7/4 - 5√7 t/4).\nD·(C-A) = (9/4+15t/4)(15/4) + (5√7/4-5√7t/4)(-5√7/4) = 0.\n(15/4)(9/4+15t/4) - (5√7/4)(5√7/4-5√7t/4)=0\n= (15/4)(9+15t)/4 - (5√7/4)·5√7(1-t)/4\n= 15(9+15t)/16 - 25·7(1-t)/16\n= [15(9+15t)-175(1-t)]/16\n= [135+225t-175+175t]/16\n= [-40+400t]/16 = 0\n→ t=40/400=1/10.\nD = (9/4+15/(40), 5√7/4-5√7/(40)) = (9/4+3/8, 5√7/4-√7/8) = (18/8+3/8, 10√7/8-√7/8) = (21/8, 9√7/8).\n\nFind E: foot of perpendicular from C=(6,0) to line AB.\nA=(9/4,5√7/4), B=(0,0). Direction AB = B-A = (-9/4,-5√7/4) or A-B=(9/4,5√7/4). Line AB through origin with direction (9/4,5√7/4), i.e., direction (9,5√7).\nE on AB: E = s·(9,5√7) (using direction from B). Actually let E = λ(9/4,5√7/4) for some λ (since B is origin, A corresponds to λ=1).\nCE ⊥ AB: (E-C)·(9/4,5√7/4)=0.\nE-C = (9λ/4-6, 5√7λ/4).\n(9λ/4-6)(9/4)+(5√7λ/4)(5√7/4)=0\n81λ/16-54/4+175λ/16=0\n(81+175)λ/16-54/4=0\n256λ/16=54/4\n16λ=54/4 → λ=54/64=27/32.\nE = (9·27/(4·32), 5√7·27/(4·32)) = (243/128, 135√7/128).\n\nNow line PD: P=(45/22,27√7/22), D=(21/8,9√7/8).\nFind intersection X with BC (the x-axis, y=0).\n\nLine through P and D. Parametrize: P + u(D-P).\nD-P = (21/8-45/22, 9√7/8-27√7/22).\n21/8-45/22: common denom 88. 21·11/88-45·4/88=231/88-180/88=51/88.\n9√7/8-27√7/22 = √7(9/8-27/22)=√7(99/88-108/88)=√7(-9/88)=-9√7/88.\nSo D-P=(51/88,-9√7/88).\n\nPoint = (45/22+51u/88, 27√7/22-9√7u/88).\nSet y=0: 27√7/22-9√7u/88=0 → 27/22=9u/88 → u=27·88/(22·9)=27·4/9=12. So u=12.\nx = 45/22+51·12/88 = 45/22+612/88 = 45/22+153/22 = 198/22=9.\nSo X=(9,0).\n\nNow line PE: P=(45/22,27√7/22), E=(243/128,135√7/128).\nE-P = (243/128-45/22, 135√7/128-27√7/22).\n243/128-45/22: common denom 1408. 243·11/1408-45·64/1408=2673/1408-2880/1408=-207/1408.\n135√7/128-27√7/22=√7(135/128-27/22)=√7(135·22-27·128)/(128·22)=√7(2970-3456)/2816=√7(-486)/2816=-486√7/2816=-243√7/1408.\nSo E-P=(-207/1408,-243√7/1408).\n\nPoint = (45/22-207u/1408, 27√7/22-243√7u/1408).\nSet y=0: 27√7/22=243√7u/1408 → 27/22=243u/1408 → u=27·1408/(22·243)=1408/(22·9)=1408/198=704/99.\nx=45/22-207·(704/99)/1408 = 45/22-207·704/(99·1408).\n207·704/(99·1408): 704/1408=1/2. So =207/(99·2)=207/198=23/22.\nx=45/22-23/22=22/22=1.\nSo Y=(1,0).\n\nNow triangle AXY: A=(9/4,5√7/4), X=(9,0), Y=(1,0).\nBase XY on x-axis from x=1 to x=9, length=8. Height = y-coordinate of A = 5√7/4.\nArea = (1/2)·8·(5√7/4)=4·5√7/4=5√7.\nArea² = 25·7=175.\n\nSo the square of the area is 175.\n\nLet me double-check X and Y computations.\n\nX: line PD with y=0. P=(45/22, 27√7/22)≈(2.045, 3.243). D=(21/8,9√7/8)≈(2.625, 2.976). Both have positive y, line going down-right slightly. To reach y=0 need to go further in direction D-P (which has negative y component -9√7/88). u=12 gives x=9. Seems far but consistent with small slope. Slope of PD = (-9√7/88)/(51/88)=-9√7/51=-3√7/17. From P, to drop y by 27√7/22≈3.243, need Δx = 3.243/(3√7/17)... slope is dy/dx=-3√7/17, so Δx=Δy/slope=(0-27√7/22)/(-3√7/17)=(27√7/22)(17/(3√7))=27·17/(22·3)=459/66=6.9545. x=2.045+6.955=9.0. ✓.\n\nY: line PE. P≈(2.045,3.243), E≈(1.898, 2.786). E-P≈(-0.147,-0.457). Slope=(-243√7/1408)/(-207/1408)=243√7/207=81√7/69=27√7/23. From P to y=0: Δy=-27√7/22, Δx=Δy/slope=(-27√7/22)/(27√7/23)=-23/22. x=45/22-23/22=22/22=1. ✓.\n\nArea = (1/2)|det([X-Y, A-Y])|... X-Y=(8,0), A-Y=(9/4-1,5√7/4)=(5/4,5√7/4). det=8·5√7/4-0=10√7. Area=5√7. Area²=175. ✓.\n\nThe answer is 175.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786706329}
